WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.157
This query converts numeric quality scores into broad bands and counts customers in each band.

00:00:06.157 --> 00:00:09.897
A summary like this can help prioritize review.

00:00:09.897 --> 00:00:13.607
But the band does not replace the underlying dimensions.

00:00:13.607 --> 00:00:19.347
If a row has a low score, you should still be able to explain whether the problem is

00:00:19.347 --> 00:00:23.567
missingness, invalid contact data, timeliness, or something else.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:28.517
Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:32.922
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention;

00:00:32.922 --> 00:00:35.497
it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:35.497 --> 00:00:42.440
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
